{
    "background_story": "In the dark depths of the ocean, Ariel was a mermaid with a sinister secret. She was the last of a ancient tribe that had been cursed by the sea goddess for their dark rituals. The curse had twisted their hunger, forcing them to cannibalize their own kind to survive. Ariel struggled to resist the primal urge, but the temptation grew stronger with each passing day. She began to hunt her own kin, luring them with enchanting songs and devouring them in the darkness. As the years went by, Ariel's powers grew, but so did her isolation. She became a monster, feared by all who crossed her path. The ocean itself seemed to whisper warnings of her presence, and sailors avoided the waters where Ariel was said to roam, forever bound to the curse that had consumed her tribe.",
